export const LLMS = "# Heuremen LLC\n\n> Heuremen LLC measures published claims against the data behind them. Quantum hardware studies are recounted against IBM's published calibration (QIA). Language-model evaluation studies are recounted from their own released files (IRIS). University AI policy documents are indexed against their own published numbers (OY). Built infrastructure is mapped from public data, with a source for every dot (ATLAS). Vendor statements about AI hardware are held against published MLPerf\u00ae results (the MODEL desk of HERMES). Every live desk is listed below with one line. Every row has a source. Data downloads are free.\n\n## API and MCP\n- [MCP server](https://indahl.ai/mcp): read-only tools over every live desk, for Claude and other agents. Add it as a remote MCP server at https://indahl.ai/mcp.\n- [REST API](https://indahl.ai/api): the same tools as JSON at /api/v1, with an OpenAPI file at /api/openapi.json. Retrieval and answering are permitted, training is not.\n\n## Divisions\n- [QIA](https://indahl.ai/qia): IBM processors measured against their published calibration, the studies calibrated, and the List of every indexed study with its receipt.\n- [IRIS](https://indahl.ai/iris): Recount Matrix for language models, live Faults and Guards runs on open models, and the List of indexed evaluation studies.\n- [OY](https://indahl.ai/oy): Learning research, school AI policy and data, recounted with a source per row.\n- [ATLAS](https://indahl.ai/atlas): Built infrastructure. A map of United States data centers from OpenStreetMap and Epoch AI, with a source and pull date for every dot.\n- [HERMES](https://indahl.ai/hermes): Held Every Record, Measured Every Statement. The menu of every division and desk.\n- [STACK](https://indahl.ai/stack): Every test side by side, live.\n\n## Desks\n### IRIS\n- [LAB](https://indahl.ai/iris/lab): Our own model runs: Sage V training live, the house training, Falcon training, the finalists, Faults and Guards across models.\n- [YO](https://indahl.ai/yo): Our small language model trained on IBM calibration records: live reads and every test.\n- [HFSIZE](https://indahl.ai/hfsize): Model names against the weights.\n- [HFLICENSE](https://indahl.ai/hflicense): Stated licenses against license files.\n- [PKGLICENSE](https://indahl.ai/pkglicense): Package licenses against repository licenses.\n- [PKGINSTALL](https://indahl.ai/pkginstall): Install commands against pip resolution.\n- [WEIGHTS](https://indahl.ai/weights): Model names against their weight files, pass after pass.\n- [AILUMINATE](https://indahl.ai/ailuminate): MLCommons AILuminate Safety results, kept and checked.\n- [HOSTS](https://indahl.ai/hosts): One open-weight model, many hosts, stated uptime and quantization.\n### OY\n- [CAMPUS](https://indahl.ai/campus): The documents behind the OY page, kept over time.\n### ATLAS\n- [ELECTRICITY](https://indahl.ai/atlas/electricity): Prices, providers and generation by state.\n- [POWER PLANTS](https://indahl.ai/atlas/power-plants): Every operating plant by fuel and capacity.\n- [CARBON](https://indahl.ai/atlas/carbon): Pounds of CO2 per megawatthour by state and grid region.\n- [PLANNED PLANTS](https://indahl.ai/atlas/planned-plants): What is coming, by fuel, stage and year.\n- [UPTIME](https://indahl.ai/uptime): Vendor status pages against independent probes.\n- [TIME](https://indahl.ai/time): Public time servers, stated against delivered.\n- [CADA](https://indahl.ai/cada): Public DNS filters against fresh abuse reports.\n- [SECRECORDS](https://indahl.ai/secrecords): Security records against their own rules.\n- [SEAT](https://indahl.ai/seat): An outside seat reads our own pages.\n- [SUPPORT](https://indahl.ai/support): Stated support windows against release activity.\n- [CHANGE](https://indahl.ai/change): Announced shutdown dates, kept over time.\n### HERMES\n- [MODEL](https://indahl.ai/hermes/model): Models and the hardware they run on: vendor statements against published results, model claims rerun, studies against their released data.\n- [TRIALS](https://indahl.ai/trials): Results due against results posted, and stopped trials.\n- [HPT](https://indahl.ai/hpt): Hospital price files against the rule.\n- [AIRLINE](https://indahl.ai/airline): Scheduled flight time against flown time.\n- [AIRQ](https://indahl.ai/airq): Air sensors against the EPA's own targets.\n- [REVISE](https://indahl.ai/revise): Stated margin against later revision.\n- [FEDSEP](https://indahl.ai/fedsep): The Fed's stated ranges against outcomes.\n- [CADENCE](https://indahl.ai/cadence): Stated update schedules against delivered.\n- [FORECAST](https://indahl.ai/forecast): Stated chance against what happened.\n- [LAUNCH](https://indahl.ai/launch): Stated launch time against the time it flew.\n- [TAPE](https://indahl.ai/tape): Every page and live feed, hashed and chained, with a beacon.\n- [VAULT](https://indahl.ai/vault): A receipt for any file, or a file sealed until a date, no file stored.\n- [ARXIVDRIFT](https://indahl.ai/arxivdrift): Studies read, then revised.\n- [LINKROT](https://indahl.ai/linkrot): Stated code links against live.\n\n## Data\n- [Feed of new studies and bench rounds (Atom)](https://indahl.ai/feed.xml)\n- [QIA List (JSON)](https://indahl.ai/qia/list.json)\n- [IRIS List (JSON)](https://indahl.ai/iris/list.json)\n- [MODEL claims (JSON)](https://indahl.ai/hermes/model/claims.json) and [per-accelerator results (CSV)](https://indahl.ai/hermes/model/accelerators.csv)\n- [Datasets on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/indahl)\n- [QIA key (codes Q1 to Q23, F1 to F7)](https://indahl.ai/qia/key)\n- [IRIS key (codes L1 to L9)](https://indahl.ai/iris/key)\n\n## Free downloads (each tested, with a TESTED.md inside)\n- [QIA Research Package](https://indahl.ai/qia/package): for runs on IBM quantum hardware. Checks the calibration record a run depends on, before and after the run. The checker alone: pip install qia-check (https://pypi.org/project/qia-check/).\n- [Darkwave Correction Kit](https://indahl.ai/darkwave/kit): measures the phase turn a mid-circuit readout gives untouched qubits on your own IBM account and adds the matching virtual-Z correction. Tested on ibm_kingston.\n- [IRIS Research Package](https://indahl.ai/iris/package): for language-model evaluations. Reading sheets for parsers, flip counts between repeated runs, paired comparisons with four outcomes. The checker alone: pip install iris-check (https://pypi.org/project/iris-check/).\n- [ATLAS Data Pack](https://indahl.ai/atlas/data-pack): every ATLAS dataset as JSON, CSV and GeoJSON with sources.\n- [QIA List Pack](https://indahl.ai/qia/qia-list-pack.zip) and [IRIS List Pack](https://indahl.ai/iris/iris-list-pack.zip): every listed study as CSV, BibTeX and RIS.\n\n## Research\n- [A Readout Is Not an Idle (paper, PDF)](https://heuremen.org/a-readout-is-not-an-idle.pdf)\n- [Faults (PDF)](https://heuremen.org/faults.pdf) and [Guards (PDF)](https://heuremen.org/guards.pdf)\n- [Zenodo record](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23662284)\n- [heuremen.org](https://heuremen.org/)\n\n## Usage\n- Free to read, download and cite with attribution. Text and data mining and use as AI training data are not permitted: https://indahl.ai/terms#ai-training\n\n## Policies\n- [Privacy](https://indahl.ai/privacy), [Terms](https://indahl.ai/terms), [Security](https://indahl.ai/security), [Conflict of interest](https://indahl.ai/conflict-of-interest)\n";
